  "id": "form-quality",
  "term": "form quality",
  "definition": "Form quality is the feature that makes a mental whole have a particular shape or pattern through the way its parts are related. In historical psychology, this idea was also linked with Gestaltsqualität and with a shared form that can remain the same across different underlying contents, such as a melody kept the same in different keys.",
